# No Beta ship without express permission

Do **not** promote work to Beta unless the user clearly asks in that turn.

Forbidden without explicit ask:
- `npm run dist:win:beta` / `dist:win:beta:build-only`
- Silent-install / overwrite of the installed Beta app
- `git push` to `beta-release` (or any Beta promote remote flow)
- Editing live Beta dashboard data on `H:\Photography\Astrophotography\Dashboard` except when the user asked to fix/restore Beta data

When editing Beta dashboard JSON (only if the user asked):
- Always copy the current file into `Dashboard/backups/` first
- Never write `projects: []` over a non-empty file
- Prefer reconstructing pipeline status from on-disk Siril trees over inventing shoot rows

Allowed without a Beta ask:
- Dev work (`npm start`, repo `data/`, commits on `main` when they asked to commit)
- Saying Beta is ready and waiting for them to approve a ship

If they say “save” / “commit” only — commit. Do not also build or install Beta.
If they say “build beta” / “ship beta” / “dist beta” — that is express permission for that ship only.
